{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "or-file-text-read-2026-11-26",
		"name": "OpenRegister File Text Read API",
		"description": "A file's extracted text is served to whoever can open the file, and to no one else (change search-file-text-and-vector-facade, task 4.1; acceptance: no route returns text from a file the caller cannot open).\n\nA user uploads a one-page PDF to their own files over WebDAV. Before extraction GET /api/files/{id}/text answers 404 'not extracted yet'; the owner extracts it (POST /api/files/{id}/extract) and reads the text back (200, the run's own word from the PDF, chunkCount and extractedAt). A second user, who shares nothing with the owner, asks for the same text and gets 404 with no text, and the same answer as for a file id that does not exist, so the refusal does not tell a stranger which ids exist.\n\nThe PDF is built per run in a pre-request script (an uncompressed text stream with computed xref offsets) around a word unique to the run, so an earlier run's extraction cannot answer for this one. Self-cleaning: it removes the file and both users.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"event": [
		{
			"listen": "prerequest",
			"script": {
				"type": "text/javascript",
				"exec": [
					"pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'OCS-APIRequest', value: 'true' });"
				]
			}
		}
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "setUp: the owner of the PDF",
			"request": {
				"method": "POST",
				"header": [
					{
						"key": "OCS-APIRequest",
						"value": "true"
					},
					{
						"key": "Accept",
						"value": "application/json"
					},
					{
						"key": "Content-Type",
						"value": "application/json"
					}
				],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{base_url}}/ocs/v2.php/cloud/users?format=json",
					"host": [
						"{{base_url}}"
					],
					"path": [
						"ocs",
						"v2.php",
						"cloud",
						"users"
					],
					"query": [
						{
							"key": "format",
							"value": "json"
						}
					]
				},
				"auth": {
					"type": "basic",
					"basic": [
						{
							"key": "username",
							"value": "{{admin_user}}",
							"type": "string"
						},
						{
							"key": "password",
							"value": "{{admin_password}}",
							"type": "string"
						}
					]
				},
				"body": {
					"mode": "raw",
					"raw": "{\"userid\": \"{{ownerId}}\", \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"}"
				}
			},
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "prerequest",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"const suffix = Date.now().toString(36) + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);",
							"pm.collectionVariables.set('suffix', suffix);",
							"pm.collectionVariables.set('ownerId', 'or-text-owner-' + suffix);",
							"pm.collectionVariables.set('strangerId', 'or-text-stranger-' + suffix);",
							"pm.collectionVariables.set('userPassword', 'Tx!' + suffix + '-' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2) + 'Zq9');",
							"// A word unique to this run, so the text read back is this file's and no earlier run's.",
							"const marker = 'Zonnewijzer' + suffix.replace(/[^a-z]/g, '');",
							"pm.collectionVariables.set('marker', marker);",
							"// A one-page PDF with an uncompressed text stream, its xref offsets computed so a parser accepts it.",
							"const stream = 'BT /F1 18 Tf 72 720 Td (Het verslag noemt ' + marker + ' als kenmerk.) Tj ET';",
							"const objects = [",
							"  '<< /Type /Catalog /Pages 2 0 R >>',",
							"  '<< /Type /Pages /Kids [3 0 R] /Count 1 >>',",
							"  '<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 4 0 R >> >> /Contents 5 0 R >>',",
							"  '<< /Type /Font /Subtype /Type1 /BaseFont /Helvetica /Encoding /WinAnsiEncoding >>',",
							"  '<< /Length ' + stream.length + ' >>\\nstream\\n' + stream + '\\nendstream',",
							"];",
							"let pdf = '%PDF-1.4\\n';",
							"const offsets = [];",
							"objects.forEach((body, i) => { offsets.push(pdf.length); pdf += (i + 1) + ' 0 obj\\n' + body + '\\nendobj\\n'; });",
							"const xref = pdf.length;",
							"pdf += 'xref\\n0 ' + (objects.length + 1) + '\\n0000000000 65535 f \\n' + offsets.map(o => String(o).padStart(10, '0') + ' 00000 n \\n').join('');",
							"pdf += 'trailer\\n<< /Size ' + (objects.length + 1) + ' /Root 1 0 R >>\\nstartxref\\n' + xref + '\\n%%EOF\\n';",
							"pm.collectionVariables.set('pdf', pdf);"
						]
					}
				},
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"pm.test('the owner is created', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code, pm.response.text()).to.eql(200));"
						]
					}
				}
			],
			"protocolProfileBehavior": {
				"disableCookies": true
			}
		},
